Bristol Reuse Campaign is a local community that aims at:
- incentivize reuse over recycling;
- create central marketing of reused goods;
- avoid massive fly-tipping and dumping of illegal waste; 
- create awareness of reuse among the local community;

To establish a more sustainable society in Bristol (UK), the Bristol Reuse Campaign is trying to modify the local ill-system into a collaborative community where people can purchasing second hand or repurposed items instead of buying them new.